  "description": "The All tasks place (docs/all-tasks.md): every open task in one list, so a task filed into an area without a day can always be found. 'groups': the tasks it shows for 'query', grouped by area. A task shows when it is open and not deleted, and every word of the query (split on spaces) is in its title or notes, ignoring case and accents; an empty query keeps them all. A project item (a task with a 'project') shows only when 'projectItems' is true. A task's group is its own area, else its project's area ('projects' maps a project id to its area), else no area. Groups come in the order of 'areas' (the order the area pickers use), with the no-area group (area null) last; an area whose id is not in 'areas' counts as no area, and an empty group is left out. Inside a group, tasks come by their date (the deadline, else the planned day), earliest first and undated last, then by title ignoring case and accents, then by id. Tasks without a 'title' use their id; 'notes', 'day', 'deadline', 'area' and 'project' are empty when left out. The area and tag filter (lists.json, 'filter') runs before these rules.",
